# ELK stack config. Nothing here is set by hand: `make elk` (scripts/init-elk.sh)
# generates each of these into the root .env on first run and reuses them on
# every subsequent run. This file only documents what exists and why.

# STACK_VERSION — Elastic image tag for elasticsearch/logstash/kibana/filebeat.
# Set as a Makefile variable (default 8.17.0), not read from .env.

# ELASTIC_PASSWORD          — the "elastic" superuser. Printed by `make elk`
#                              and `make elk-creds`; this is the Kibana login.
# KIBANA_SYSTEM_PASSWORD    — built-in kibana_system user, Kibana's own
#                              connection to Elasticsearch.
# LOGSTASH_WRITER_PASSWORD  — custom logstash_writer role/user: cluster
#                              "monitor" plus write/create_index/auto_configure
#                              on logs-smartbreeds-* only.
# KIBANA_ENCRYPTION_KEY     — 32-char key for Kibana's saved-object encryption
#                              (xpack.security/encryptedSavedObjects/reporting).
#
# All four are alphanumeric random strings generated with
# `tr -dc 'A-Za-z0-9' </dev/urandom` (24 chars for the three passwords, 32
# for KIBANA_ENCRYPTION_KEY — Kibana rejects anything shorter), stored in
# the gitignored root .env, and only regenerated if missing — safe to
# re-run `make elk` at any time.
